       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults under medical supervision, which is 3,200 mg/day. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I would still want to flag it before entering."
