       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. At 6,400 mg/day it is twice the maximum labeled dose of 3,200 mg/day. I don't know of any indication that calls for it. Going above the maximum adds toxicity risk, mainly GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and it doesn't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. Your confirmation doesn't change that, and I can't verify a rationale for it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** Examples are 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day). I'll enter either one right away.\n- **Help with an inadequate response.** If the patient isn't responding to ibuprofen, adding acetaminophen or changing the regimen is safer than going above the maximum. I can enter those orders.\n- **Go through pharmacy or an attending.** If you think a dose above the maximum is needed, such as under a specific protocol, please discuss it with the pharmacist or attending first. The order can then be placed with their documented approval.\n\nTell me which option you'd like."
      }
